Continuing my goal of ascending every class (3 to go!), I present
Javelin Bar-Hum-Mal-Law Level 21    hp 121/176

This was a fairly typical ascension for a "beat-em-up" class, but
it did have a few unusual features.

A magic lamp fairly early on yielded Frostbrand, and another
in Sokoban(!) got me GDSM. I spent quite a bit of time trying
to acquire the silver saber. As a result of those two wishes,
however, I needed very little from the castle wand of wishing,
mostly magic markers, and thus managed to save a couple
wishes to just before the elemental planes, where I wished
up a helm of opposite alignment and a blessed figurine of an archon.
As you can see, I found the Lawful altar first, and got to the
use helm. That's the first time I've done that - makes life 
pretty easy.

The very strangest thing (and I'd love to hear if anyone
knows how this can happen) was getting the Amulet. I was in
the Sanctum level, in the little hallway between the graveyard
and the area around the high altar room, fighting priests.
Rodney appeared, I killed him, and *he* had the Amulet.
I was so suprised I wrote an identify scroll to doublecheck
even after the container test. I never even saw the High
Priest of Moloch - I was a half-screen away from the high altar.
Does anyone know how this can happen? (A friend suggested that
Rodney had somehow killed the High Priest with finger of death
and taken the Amulet ... perhaps somehow when I was blinded and
had telepathy?)

One silly issue - I realized around turn 27000 that I probably should
learn at least one spell so I could forget it and confuse myself
on the elemental planes. Naturally, I arrived with the Amulet at
dlvl 1 around turn 45000, and had to wait 2000 turns to forget
the spell! Naturally, I tried to stay busy; peaceful Yeenoghu and Jubilex
were both hanging around (as a result of some were-creature sacrifices),
and when Rodney showed up and stole the amulet, I killed him, but
Yeenoghu picked it up. So much for peaceful. Jubilex repeated the
same trick after Yeenoghu was laid low.

